From f95470f3fb79be2f079652f19f99639f5322d3a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:30:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(viz): union the two inline-3D rect channels per element,
 not all-or-nothing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A tile rendered raw side-by-side — neither woven nor suppressed — while every
other tile on the page wove correctly: 6 weave rects for 7 visible elements.

Both failures have one cause, because both the weave and the canvas-quad
suppression are driven by the same list: the element was missing from
SurfaceAggregator's inline_3d_rects_ entirely.

There are two channels feeding that list. The compositor-thread tracked-element
rects (kInline3dWeave) are preferred because cc projects them through the
layer's ScreenSpaceTransform at draw time, so they match the presented pixels
exactly. The legacy channel is Blink's main-thread getBoundingClientRect
snapshot patched by an approximate impl-scroll delta (patch 0056). The fallback
between them was all-or-nothing:

    if (!has_tracked_inline3d) { ...legacy... }

But the channels do not necessarily describe the same SET of elements. The
tracked channel only carries a canvas cc registered a tracked element for on
THIS frame, so a canvas that momentarily has none — a resize that re-rasters or
re-layers it is how we hit this — drops out of the weave the instant ANY OTHER
inline-3D canvas reports a tracked rect. One element suppresses the fallback for
all of them, so the failure gets MORE likely the more 3D content a page has, and
the surviving tiles look perfect, which is what makes it read as an
identity-matching bug rather than a missing rect.

Take the union instead, per element. The reliable signal is how many elements
each channel describes, not where it thinks they are — a geometric test is not
safe here, because the two channels are measured at different times on different
threads and mid-fling they separate by more than half a tile:

  legacy_count <= tracked_count  =>  admit NOTHING. By pigeonhole the tracked
  channel already describes at least as many elements, so none is missing and
  any geometric disagreement is a measurement delta. This is the steady state,
  scrolling included.

  legacy_count >  tracked_count  =>  admit exactly the difference, picking WHICH
  by a 1:1 greedy join: every legacy rect claims its best overlapping unclaimed
  tracked rect, strongest pairings first, and the ones left with no partner at
  all are the genuinely missing elements. A displaced rect still claims its
  partner — it remains that partner's best match once the centres have parted —
  so a scroll delta can no longer promote a duplicate to "missing".

Two rects for one element is worse than the miss the union was written to fix:
both get woven and both get suppressed, so the trailing duplicate lands the
weave over whatever 2D content has scrolled under it. That is not hypothetical —
with SurfaceControl overlay promotion off, the element that motivated the union
IS tracked (device log: tracked=7, legacy_admitted=1, total=8), so a
centre-containment rule was adding a near-duplicate, not a missing element.

Overlap is scored against the SMALLER of the two areas, so a clip or a scroll
delta lowers the score without breaking the pairing and a neighbouring tile
cannot swallow one whole. The join stays geometric because the legacy channel
carries no token — the same "no identity => geometric matching" contract the
consumers implement. An admitted legacy rect keeps browser#117's
root_target_clip_rect for the same reason the tracked channel does: the
consumer's join scores it against an unclipped quad rect on the same terms.

The existing dedup pass cannot do this job: it only collapses ADJACENT
duplicates with equal NON-ZERO ids, and legacy rects are zero-id by
construction, so simply making the fallback unconditional would have
double-added every element.

Not superseded by 0072-0074: those fix a tile going DARK (a resolve/suppress set
asymmetry and a lost read-access race); this fixes a tile that is in neither list
and renders raw side-by-side. Different failure, still live.

Logs once, latched, and only when the channels actually disagree — carrying the
cardinalities that drove the decision.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Lf6vUbdL59MqXMwJxB489
---
 .../viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc | 168 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 159 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
index d371abb49ec5e..53026b9893e3a 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
@@ -2978,6 +2978,11 @@ void SurfaceAggregator::CollectTrackedElementRects(
   // getBoundingClientRect snapshot patched by an approximate impl-scroll delta
   // and trail during a fling.
   bool has_tracked_inline3d = false;
+  // Where THIS surface's tracked weave rects start, so the legacy pass below
+  // can tell "already covered by a tracked rect" from "covered by some other
+  // surface's rect".
+  const size_t tracked_begin = inline_3d_rects_.size();
+  size_t tracked_metadata_count = 0;
   for (const auto& [feature, tracked_elements] :
        frame_metadata.tracked_element_rects) {
     if (feature == TrackedElementFeature::kInline3dWeave) {
@@ -2985,6 +2990,7 @@ void SurfaceAggregator::CollectTrackedElementRects(
       // don't leak into CopyOutput geometry or the pixel-moving-filter union.
       // Skip empty rects (fully-clipped/offscreen canvases) — an empty rect
       // must never suppress the legacy fallback below or reach the weave.
+      tracked_metadata_count += tracked_elements.size();
       for (const auto& rect_data : tracked_elements) {
         if (rect_data.visible_bounds.IsEmpty()) {
           continue;
@@ -3018,21 +3024,165 @@ void SurfaceAggregator::CollectTrackedElementRects(
       tracked_element_rects_[feature].push_back(transformed_rect_data);
     }
   }
-  // DisplayXR inline-3D (#625, Step B / B4b): legacy main-thread-measured rects
-  // — used only when this frame carries no tracked-element weave rects, so the
-  // old path stays a live fallback and nothing regresses.
-  if (!has_tracked_inline3d) {
-    for (const gfx::Rect& rect : frame_metadata.inline_3d_rects) {
+  // DisplayXR inline-3D (#625, Step B / B4b): legacy main-thread-measured
+  // rects, as a PER-ELEMENT fallback.
+  //
+  // This used to be all-or-nothing — `if (!has_tracked_inline3d)` — and that is
+  // a real defect, not a simplification. The two channels do not necessarily
+  // describe the same SET of elements: the tracked channel only carries a
+  // canvas that cc registered a tracked element for on THIS frame, so a canvas
+  // that momentarily has none (a resize that re-rasters or re-layers it is the
+  // way we hit this) vanishes from the weave entirely the instant ANY OTHER
+  // inline-3D canvas reports a tracked rect. It is then neither woven nor
+  // suppressed, so the page shows its raw side-by-side — which is exactly the
+  // reported symptom: 6 weave rects for 7 visible elements, one tile in raw SBS
+  // while the rest weave correctly. Every additional 3D element on the page
+  // makes it MORE likely, because it only takes one to suppress the fallback
+  // for all of them.
+  //
+  // So take the union instead — but as a CARDINALITY question, not a geometric
+  // one. The first cut of this fix admitted any legacy rect no tracked rect
+  // centre-contained, and that is unsafe during a scroll, which is when it
+  // matters most. The two channels are measured at different times in different
+  // threads: the legacy rect is a Blink main-thread getBoundingClientRect
+  // snapshot patched by an approximate impl-scroll delta (see patch 0056), the
+  // tracked one is cc's draw-time projected visible_bounds. Mid-fling they
+  // separate by more than half a tile, centre-containment then fails for a pair
+  // that describes the SAME element, and the stale legacy rect is admitted
+  // alongside the accurate tracked one. Two rects for one element is worse than
+  // the miss this was written to fix: the consumers weave BOTH, so the trailing
+  // duplicate lands the weave over whatever 2D content has scrolled under it.
+  //
+  // The reliable signal is how many elements each channel describes, not where
+  // it thinks they are:
+  //
+  //   * legacy_count <= tracked_count  =>  admit NOTHING. By pigeonhole the
+  //     tracked channel already describes at least as many elements as the
+  //     legacy one, so no element is missing from it, and any geometric
+  //     disagreement is a measurement delta rather than a set difference. This
+  //     is the whole steady state, scrolling included.
+  //   * legacy_count >  tracked_count  =>  admit exactly the difference, and
+  //     pick WHICH by a 1:1 greedy join: every legacy rect claims its best
+  //     overlapping unclaimed tracked rect, and the leftovers — the ones with
+  //     no partner at all — are the genuinely missing elements. A displaced
+  //     rect still claims its partner (it is that partner's best match even
+  //     when the centres have parted), so a scroll delta can no longer promote
+  //     a duplicate to "missing".
+  //
+  // The join stays geometric because the legacy channel carries no token (see
+  // below) — the same "no identity => geometric matching" contract the
+  // consumers implement. Overlap is scored against the SMALLER of the two
+  // areas, so a clip or a scroll delta lowers the score without breaking the
+  // pairing, and a neighbouring tile cannot swallow one whole.
+  const size_t tracked_end = inline_3d_rects_.size();
+  const size_t tracked_count = tracked_end - tracked_begin;
+
+  std::vector<gfx::Rect> legacy_dest;
+  legacy_dest.reserve(frame_metadata.inline_3d_rects.size());
+  for (const gfx::Rect& rect : frame_metadata.inline_3d_rects) {
+    const gfx::Rect dest = TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace(
+        rect, target_transform, transform_to_root_target,
+        root_target_clip_rect);
+    if (!dest.IsEmpty()) {
+      legacy_dest.push_back(dest);
+    }
+  }
+
+  size_t legacy_admitted = 0;
+  if (legacy_dest.size() > tracked_count) {
+    // Best partner (and its score) for each legacy rect. Scores are in [0,1];
+    // -1 means "overlaps no tracked rect at all".
+    struct Cand {
+      size_t legacy_index = 0;
+      size_t tracked_index = 0;
+      float score = -1.f;
+    };
+    std::vector<Cand> cands;
+    cands.reserve(legacy_dest.size());
+    for (size_t l = 0; l < legacy_dest.size(); ++l) {
+      Cand c;
+      c.legacy_index = l;
+      for (size_t i = tracked_begin; i < tracked_end; ++i) {
+        gfx::Rect isect = inline_3d_rects_[i].rect;
+        isect.Intersect(legacy_dest[l]);
+        if (isect.IsEmpty()) {
+          continue;
+        }
+        const int64_t inter = static_cast<int64_t>(isect.width()) *
+                              static_cast<int64_t>(isect.height());
+        const int64_t a = static_cast<int64_t>(legacy_dest[l].width()) *
+                          static_cast<int64_t>(legacy_dest[l].height());
+        const int64_t b =
+            static_cast<int64_t>(inline_3d_rects_[i].rect.width()) *
+            static_cast<int64_t>(inline_3d_rects_[i].rect.height());
+        const int64_t denom = std::min(a, b);
+        const float score =
+            denom > 0 ? static_cast<float>(inter) / static_cast<float>(denom)
+                      : 0.f;
+        if (score > c.score) {
+          c.score = score;
+          c.tracked_index = i;
+        }
+      }
+      cands.push_back(c);
+    }
+    // Strongest pairings claim first, so a confident match is never displaced
+    // by a weaker one competing for the same tracked rect.
+    std::stable_sort(cands.begin(), cands.end(),
+                     [](const Cand& x, const Cand& y) {
+                       return x.score > y.score;
+                     });
+    std::vector<bool> claimed(tracked_end - tracked_begin, false);
+    std::vector<bool> admit(legacy_dest.size(), false);
+    size_t budget = legacy_dest.size() - tracked_count;
+    for (const Cand& c : cands) {
+      if (c.score > 0.f && !claimed[c.tracked_index - tracked_begin]) {
+        claimed[c.tracked_index - tracked_begin] = true;
+        continue;
+      }
+      // No partner left (or none ever). This is a genuinely missing element —
+      // up to the budget, which can never be exceeded by construction.
+      if (budget > 0) {
+        admit[c.legacy_index] = true;
+        --budget;
+      }
+    }
+    for (size_t l = 0; l < legacy_dest.size(); ++l) {
+      if (!admit[l]) {
+        continue;
+      }
       // Phase-1 identity: the legacy main-thread channel carries no element
       // token and no layer id. Zeroes here are the documented "no identity"
       // signal — the consumer falls back to geometric matching and to
       // positional per-target state, i.e. exactly today's behaviour.
       inline_3d_rects_.push_back(
-          {TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace(rect, target_transform,
-                                              transform_to_root_target,
-                                              root_target_clip_rect),
-           base::Token(), /*sqs_layer_id=*/0u, std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t>(),
+          {legacy_dest[l], base::Token(), /*sqs_layer_id=*/0u,
+           std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t>(),
+           // browser#117: an admitted legacy rect keeps the same clip the
+           // tracked channel keeps, so the consumer's join scores it against
+           // an unclipped quad rect on the same terms.
            root_target_clip_rect});
+      ++legacy_admitted;
+    }
+  }
+
+  // Latched, and only when the two channels actually disagree — this is the
+  // shape of the bug above, so say so once rather than leaving it to be
+  // inferred from a tile that looks wrong.
+  if (legacy_admitted > 0 && has_tracked_inline3d) {
+    static bool logged_union = false;
+    if (!logged_union) {
+      logged_union = true;
+      LOG(WARNING) << "[DisplayXR] inline-3D rect union: tracked="
+                   << tracked_count << " (of " << tracked_metadata_count
+                   << " reported) legacy_metadata="
+                   << frame_metadata.inline_3d_rects.size()
+                   << " legacy_nonempty=" << legacy_dest.size()
+                   << " legacy_admitted=" << legacy_admitted
+                   << " total=" << inline_3d_rects_.size()
+                   << " — element(s) missing from the tracked channel were "
+                      "recovered from the main-thread channel; without this "
+                      "they would render as raw SBS";
     }
   }
 }
